2. BRD Requirements (Verbatim)
Requirement ID	Category	Priority	Requirement (Verbatim from BRD)
REQ-001	Functional	High	The system must validate DQM quoted orders to ensure they have a deal reference and at least one UCID.
REQ-002	Functional	High	During quote load, the system must compare the deal version on the quote with the latest version available in S4.
REQ-003	Functional	High	If the deal version on the quote differs from the S4 response, the order processing must stop immediately and move to R&R.
REQ-004	Functional	High	The system must display a message indicating the version mismatch, showing both the quote's deal version and the latest S4 deal version.
REQ-005	Functional	High	Upon passing the deal version check, the system must validate UCID net prices against the S4 response.
REQ-006	Functional	High	If any UCID has a different net price than expected, the order must also be stopped in R&R.
REQ-007	Functional	Medium	The system should provide a business-readable reason for stopping an order due to UCID net price inconsistencies.
REQ-008	Non-Functional	High	The validation outcome must be persisted for audit and troubleshooting purposes.
REQ-009	Technical	High	The system must log S4 interaction details, including correlation references, whenever a quote is processed.
REQ-010	Performance	Medium	The validation checks must complete during quote load to minimize processing delays.
REQ-011	Constraint	High	Validation checks are only required during quote load and not during quote conversion.
REQ-012	Assumption	Medium	The validation process is applicable to both manual and electronic orders originating from DQM.
REQ-013	Constraint	High	Non-DQM flows, quotes without a deal reference, and quotes without UCID must be explicitly excluded from validation.
REQ-014	Non-Functional	Medium	The system must handle service failure scenarios, ensuring that if S4 does not respond or returns incomplete data, the quote does not proceed silently.
REQ-015	Technical	Medium	The system must ensure consistent behavior for repeated quote loads, even in the event of failure scenarios.
